Fixed. Both typecheck and tests pass.

The bug was on line 43 of `src/sim.ts`:

```js
if (foodSurplus >= 0) {   // ← was growing population at break-even
```

`foodSurplus` is `foodProduced - foodConsumed`. A settlement "just barely breaking even on food" has `foodSurplus === 0`, but the `>= 0` check treated that as growth-worthy. Changed it to a strict inequality so population only grows on a genuine surplus:

```js
if (foodSurplus > 0) {   // ← grows only when production exceeds consumption
```

This matches the function's own docstring ("grows by 1 if there was a food surplus this turn") and stops the turn-after-turn growth in break-even settlements. Verified with `npm run typecheck` (passed) and `npm run test` (4 passed).


